// Both sides must refuse a nesting depth past 200, with matching error
// messages and exit codes. This probe confirms LoxOps.Stringify's depth
// guard (issue #159's real fix) keeps native and CLR in sync.
//
// Native: list 200 prints OK, list 201 throws LoxError("Value nesting is
// too deep."), exit 70.
// CLR: same depth, same result, same message.
//
// Without the CLR guard, native would reject and exit 70 while CLR would
// print the full nested structure on a 256 MiB thread (tools/clr_run.sh's
// default), a divergence caught by tools/check_clr_probes.sh's error_probes
// loop: "CLR run did not fail".

print "before";
var x = 0;
var n = 0;
while (n < 201) {
    x = [x];
    n = n + 1;
}
print x;
